WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:05.180
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here
and in this video, I'm revealing ten characters

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:09.680
Pixar cut from Incredibles 2 who you might
wish had been included in the movie.

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:13.260
If you're joining me for the first time, be
sure to tap the bell to get my new videos

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:17.220
and also leave a comment about the movie for
a chance to win an awesome Funko Pop.

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:20.812
Spoilers ahead, so take care if you've not
seen the film, or add this video to your Watch

00:00:20.812 --> 00:00:21.999
Later playlist.

00:00:21.999 --> 00:00:26.689
Although we never saw her and only briefly
heard her voice, Frozone's wife Honey was

00:00:26.689 --> 00:00:31.970
a huge hit with fans in the first movie, so
much so that that Pixar used her only moment

00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:34.100
in the sequel to promote the film in the trailer.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.700
"Where you going asap?"

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:37.700
"You better be back asap!"

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:42.239
Sadly, that's about as much as fans got of
Honey in Incredibles 2 but we could have had

00:00:42.239 --> 00:00:44.969
more as she very nearly made it on screen.

00:00:44.969 --> 00:00:48.860
The filmmakers said they not only created
a design for Honey, but they also initially

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:51.380
included her in the movie's opening sequence.

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:55.900
Unfortunately, the scene was scrapped as writer-director
Brad Bird felt it didn't fit and the movie

00:00:55.900 --> 00:01:01.309
was already too packed, so once again we only
get to hear Honey's voice in the sequel, which

00:01:01.309 --> 00:01:02.910
Bird believes is funnier.

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:07.330
It's a real shame that Honey didn't get to
make her on-screen debut as I know many Pixar

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:09.720
fans were hoping she'd make an appearance.

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:13.010
The storyboard of Honey's deleted cameo will
be on the Blu-ray.

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:17.170
And her design was re-used in the movie for
one of the many supers assembled on the yacht

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:18.170
at the end.

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:23.140
Look for the character with pink hair, bluish-coloured
suit and long gloves plus goggles.

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:27.250
When Edna Mode discovers that Elastigirl's
new super-suit was created by a designer called

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:30.060
Alexander Galbaki, she's absolutely furious!

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:33.220
"Elastigirl's super suit is by Galbaki!"

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:35.380
"Explain yourself!"

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:40.710
Now, Galbaki only gets a name-check in the
final film, but originally, Edna's rival super-suit

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:45.820
designer was actually going to appear on screen
in a suit-fitting scene with Elastigirl.

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:50.070
Galbaki's character was meant to deliberately
contrast with Edna as his designs were all

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:54.070
about showing off and drawing attention to
him as a designer rather than focusing on

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:56.610
the needs of the supers he's designing for.

00:01:56.610 --> 00:02:00.920
And as if that wasn't enough to get Edna's
blood boiling, his designs even broke her

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:01.960
golden rule.

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:03.070
"No capes!"

00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:06.810
Giving Elastigirl a cape that she clearly
didn't like or need.

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:12.280
Some early designs of Helen riding the Elasticycle
show her wearing a cape at the same time.

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:16.530
Wearing capes while close to incredibly fast
spinning objects is clearly something that's

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:19.730
very dangerous, as we saw in the first movie!

00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:24.250
A character that many fans would like to have
seen return for the sequel was Kari the babysitter.

00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:28.980
Kari's role from the first movie was expanded
when she featured in the short film Jack-Jack

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:33.990
Attack which showed her discovering baby Parr's
superpowers and then having her memory wiped

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:35.530
by Rick Dicker.

00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:40.060
And the filmmakers appear to have had a brief
cameo in mind for her in the sequel as concept

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:44.380
art of Kari and her parents appears in the
Art of Incredibles 2 hardback book.

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:49.130
In an earlier version of the movie, Winston
Deavor didn't have a sister, instead he had

00:02:49.130 --> 00:02:52.130
a brother called Nelson who was the original
villain.

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:55.990
As the story progressed though, Brad Bird
decided the villain would actually work better

00:02:55.990 --> 00:02:57.450
as a female character.

00:02:57.450 --> 00:03:01.760
So, the decision was made to scrap Winston's
brother and instead introduce a sister called

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:02.760
Evelyn.

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:06.600
And as a bonus, the team found they were able
to make the relationship between Evelyn and

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:10.930
Helen stronger and more interesting than they
were with Nelson and Elastigirl.

00:03:10.930 --> 00:03:16.400
Nelson's design wasn't totally lost though
and he was re-used as the wannabe super He-Lectrix.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:20.319
And before He-Lectrix, there was originally
a female version of this lightning-powered

00:03:20.319 --> 00:03:21.680
super called She-lectric.

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:27.290
She-lectric's design ended up being used for
Evelyn who, as I mentioned, was made the main

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:29.020
villain for the movie.

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:32.800
While we do get lots of new super-powered
characters in the movie, even more supers

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:35.599
were designed for the film but didn't make
the final cut.

00:03:35.599 --> 00:03:39.770
For example, Brad Bird mentioned a character
called "Overthink" who was originally going

00:03:39.770 --> 00:03:44.330
to be a bigger part of the film but ended
up only appearing very briefly with the international

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:47.630
supers at the end of the movie and who was
never named.

00:03:47.630 --> 00:03:52.599
According to Bird, "his power was incredible
mental energy, but he takes time to consider

00:03:52.599 --> 00:03:56.709
every single thing, and usually misses his
opportunity to correct whatever the problem

00:03:56.709 --> 00:03:59.970
was because there's always one more angle
to explore"!

00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:05.320
The whole idea of an overthinking superpower
seems a bit strange as it sounds less of a

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:07.550
superpower and more of a chronic weakness.

00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:11.600
I can see the humorous potential but it sounds
like the character might have been a bit too

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:14.459
complicated to get across on screen.

00:04:14.459 --> 00:04:18.629
Another secondary superhero that appears in
the outtakes section of the Art of Incredibles

00:04:18.629 --> 00:04:20.359
2 book is Cosmosis.

00:04:20.359 --> 00:04:24.570
Judging from his name and the many celestial
designs considered for his super-suit, I'd

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:29.199
say he was probably going to have various
powers of cosmic manipulation.

00:04:29.199 --> 00:04:33.240
Cosmic powers can endow users with powerful
abilities such as manipulating matter across

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:38.830
space and time, and creating force fields
or portals between locations and dimensions.

00:04:38.830 --> 00:04:43.319
Cosmosis could have been on a par with extremely
powerful superheroes like Captain Marvel and

00:04:43.319 --> 00:04:45.210
Jean Grey's Phoenix Force.

00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:50.560
If Cosmosis was only meant to be a secondary
superhero or a wannabe super like Voyd and

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:53.100
her crew, then I think he was probably cut
from the movie because he might have been

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:58.139
too formidable an opponent for the Incredibles
family and even the extremely over-powered

00:04:58.139 --> 00:04:59.460
Jack-Jack.

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:04.040
The filmmakers had yet more ideas for supers
they hoped to introduce in the sequel.

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:08.120
There was Berserkeley, who reminds me a bit
of Batman villain Poison Ivy with the green

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:10.589
mask and leaf-like cape behind her.

00:05:10.589 --> 00:05:14.840
And her name suggests she might have some
wild or out-of-control powers.

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:18.509
Shock-N-Awe are a pair of supers and their
name and hairstyles suggest they have some

00:05:18.509 --> 00:05:20.930
kind of electrical or lightning powers.

00:05:20.930 --> 00:05:25.090
The purplish colours in their hair and glasses
made me think of the Wonder Twins from Super

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:28.650
Friends, however, they don't share similar
powers with that DC duo.

00:05:28.650 --> 00:05:32.999
The deleted trio Megaman &amp; Co seem to be the
least developed of the supers design-wise

00:05:32.999 --> 00:05:37.000
and look like they're wearing home-made costumes,
so it's possible they were going to be used

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:40.240
more for comic effect than any real threat
to the Incredibles.

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:43.919
Now, do you wish any of these characters had
appeared in the movie?

